# SCRATCH (docs/plans/BOUNCE-BONANZA-WALLCLOCK.md): host blocks for a wall clock, compiled only by
# wallclock.py, never shipped.  A floor apron round three blocks, each 2 x 2 cells, so both of a block's
# visible faces (sw: the left, the +y face; se: the right, the +x face) are two cells wide and in full view:
# 3 units (24 px), 2 units (16 px) and 1 unit (8 px) proud.
course WALLT "Wall clock test"
width 96
ball rubber
floor rect 3 3 20 11 flat 0
floor rect 5 6 7 8 flat 3
floor rect 10 6 12 8 flat 2
floor rect 15 6 17 8 flat 1
goal  rect 19 10 20 11 flat 0
start 4 4
